{
 "book": "1 Nephi",
 "chapter": 6,
 "intro": "Chapter 6 is Nephi's brief editorial aside. Interrupting the narrative, he explains why he will **not** copy his fathers' full genealogy or a complete history onto these plates: that record already exists on his father's plates, and the room here is limited. His purpose, he says, is spiritual rather than historical — to **persuade all people to come unto the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob and be saved**. He therefore writes only what is pleasing to God, and commands his descendants not to fill the plates with things of no worth to the children of men.",
