    {
     "type": "grammar-note",
     "title": "Grammar: Compound verbs with کردن, شدن, دادن, یافتن",
     "body": "Persian expresses most actions by pairing a noun with a light verb that carries the tense, person, and mood. `کردن` \"do\" and `دادن` \"give\" build active senses; `شدن` \"become\" and `یافتن` \"find/obtain\" build inchoative or passive ones. The noun is the meaning; the light verb is the grammar. This short chapter is full of them.",
     "examples": [
      {
       "ref": "Chapter summary",
       "ref_anchor": "chapter-summary",
       "persian": "ترغیب کند",
       "translit": "tarġīb konad",
       "en": "may persuade (lit. \"make persuasion\")"
      },
      {
       "ref": "Chapter summary",
       "ref_anchor": "chapter-summary",
       "persian": "نجات یابند",
       "translit": "najāt yāband",
       "en": "be saved (lit. \"find salvation\")"
      },
      {
       "ref": "Verse 6",
       "ref_anchor": "verse-6",
       "persian": "فرمان می دهم",
       "translit": "farmān mī-daham",
       "en": "I command (lit. \"give a command\")"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "grammar-note",
     "title": "Grammar: The subjunctive of purpose after تا",
     "body": "`تا` \"so that, in order to\" opens a clause of **purpose**, and its verb stands in the **subjunctive** — the mood of unrealized or intended action. A simple verb takes the prefix `بـ-` (`بگویم`, `بنویسم`); a compound verb usually drops it and leaves the bare present stem (`ترغیب کنم`, `نجات یابند`). The subjunctive never takes `می-`.",
     "examples": [
      {
       "ref": "Chapter summary",
       "ref_anchor": "chapter-summary",
       "persian": "تا ... آیند و نجات یابند",
       "translit": "tā ... āyand o najāt yāband",
       "en": "that they may come and be saved"
      },
      {
       "ref": "Verse 2",
       "ref_anchor": "verse-2",
       "persian": "تا بگویم",
       "translit": "tā be-gūyam",
       "en": "to say"
      },
      {
       "ref": "Verse 4",
       "ref_anchor": "verse-4",
       "persian": "ترغیب کنم",
       "translit": "tarġīb konam",
       "en": "that I may persuade"
      }
     ]
    }
